    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Arrighetti, **Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% boost from the pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a crucial 2% bump due to the SP's slow delivery, which significantly improves his prospects for a stolen base\u2014a vital metric given our strategy to emphasize speed. Joining him at the top of our \"Strong\" tier is **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), who faces the favorable matchup against Dobnak. **Merrill** is in an ideal position to capitalize on a high-ceiling environment, buoyed by a 19% SP skill boost and a dynamic platoon advantage that makes him a must-start alongside **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.07). These four represent the core of our daily production, effectively exploiting the vulnerabilities of their respective right-handed counterparts.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the daily slate centered on **Nasim Nunez**, who posted a respectable 61.09 score but failed to crack the starting nine. While **Nunez** benefits from a park and pitcher matchup similar to **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, his projected spot at the bottom of the order (-8% penalty) tipped the scales against him in favor of our middle-of-the-order hitters. We remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Jacob Wilson**; should any of these players move down the order, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. Conversely, **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** provide excellent value today against Bieber; **Vargas** is particularly compelling with an elite 0.401 xwOBA, while **Antonacci** takes advantage of an order-driven 10% boost at the leadoff spot. We have benched **Josh Jung**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Liam Hicks** primarily to preserve our game caps, as their matchups against tough arms like Murphy and Montgomery suppressed their efficiency scores below our 40-point threshold.",
